{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-strictly-henselian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e5fc7892ed5d3c89859f320312560ac7543d92ccd56c8b74f4e03c4acf0d532c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e9d29ed81eb5d4a28e16270595f24c2b167767b9ee42e009b7cc49f9f7b421f4", "source_text": "A local ring <MATH_0001> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>strictly henselian<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it is henselian and its\nresidue field is separably closed.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2ff52583980cfbf98fe6e374a21b89855e69fe9fec7ab49e6360a681f74f64a0", "unit_id": "tag:03QK:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$R = \\mathbf{C}[[t]]$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$R \\to R$", "MATH_0004": "$R \\to R[X, X^{-1}]/(X^n-t)$", "MATH_0005": "$D(t) \\subset \\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{\\text{id} : \\Spec(R) \\to \\Spec(R)\\}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-powerseries}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e1ca696b15e562fad344d4c3563f58921181b3329489b7392685bb8d3e8c85b4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9742a882cae3d0466c2f74a2841718a63cd4864a1d02ceef3b74e6f642abb574", "source_text": "In the case <MATH_0001>, the <ACCENT_0001>tale <MATH_0002>-algebras are finite products\nof the trivial extension <MATH_0003> and the extensions\n<MATH_0004>.\nThe latter ones factor through the open <MATH_0005>, so any\n<ACCENT_0002>tale covering can be refined by the covering\n<MATH_0006>. We will see below that\nthis is a somewhat general fact on <ACCENT_0003>tale coverings of spectra of henselian\nrings. This will show that higher <ACCENT_0004>tale cohomology of the spectrum of a\nstrictly henselian ring is zero.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa01f7a0c22042899158cb9de7f017ec3714ca97ae5b504f9722f3f1838b91ee", "unit_id": "tag:03QI:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$(R, \\mathfrak m, \\kappa)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\kappa\\subset\\kappa^{sep}$", "MATH_0003": "$R \\to R^h \\to R^{sh}$", "MATH_0004": "$R^h$", "MATH_0005": "$R^{sh}$", "MATH_0006": "$R$", "MATH_0007": "$R^h$", "MATH_0008": "$R^{sh}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathfrak m R^h$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathfrak m R^{sh}$", "MATH_0011": "$R^h$", "MATH_0012": "$R^{sh}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\kappa = R^h/\\mathfrak m R^h$", "MATH_0014": "$\\kappa^{sep} = R^{sh}/\\mathfrak m R^{sh}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\kappa$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-henselization}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d3e19ee7be82d390dd8dd83696c48d6c9ce669373e302b78706e1e61d5f829c3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aa741f44da81373081a7c767abe4e0666985d501b7df4d901f8af2009f3411f4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a local ring and\n<MATH_0002> a separable algebraic closure.\nThere exist canonical flat local ring maps <MATH_0003> where\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005> are filtered colimits of <ACCENT_0001>tale <MATH_0006>-algebras,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0007> is henselian, <MATH_0008> is strictly henselian,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0009> (resp.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0010>) is the\nmaximal ideal of <MATH_0011> (resp.<SPACE_0002><MATH_0012>), and\n<STRUCT_0005> <MATH_0013>, and\n<MATH_0014> as extensions of <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8be520d91e36c9885be1939a84aa2338a37d299b4d9c7d9383413548d1a104bc", "unit_id": "tag:03QL:statement"}
