{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03QD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-henselization}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-definition-henselization}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-algebra-section-permanence-henselization}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:103c4d2b7eba8315df9a978e976ac0b41d8778b6af7fbee40f280209877d12d3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4987839d525da9b8175d6945c56b170a1778417123da2c7556cac0ef90404f5c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe rings constructed in Theorem <REF_0001>\nare called respectively the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>henselization<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> and the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>strict henselization<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> of the local ring <MATH_0001>, see\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0002>.\nMany of the properties of <MATH_0002> are reflected in its (strict) henselization,\nsee More on Algebra,\nSection <REF_0003>.\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d3baa04613907ead0dbb57c43d69418243d92f01e69eb92249c6b5027ae1139f", "unit_id": "tag:03QD:prose-0004"}
